  <prompt>
    Author a new "Communication Triage" JPS Action that produces structured output — **category, urgency, obligations[], suggested actions[], response checklist** — and deliver it via `DeliverComposite` (ADR-037 section-name-keyed streaming), following `docs/architecture/SPAARKE-PLAYBOOK-LLM-OUTPUT-PATTERN.md` (the two-layer orchestrator-template + PromptSchemaRenderer `## Input` pattern). Reuse task 031's rung-5 extract/classify Action as the input/reference where they overlap — do NOT duplicate classification logic.

    Implement per the gate-050 boundary: consume `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` seams; do NOT fork `Services/Ai/` internals. Use `jps-action-create` + `jps-validate` for the Action JSON. The rule config + tests are task 054.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke AI/JPS engineer. Authoritative on JPS Action authoring (`jps-action-create`, `jps-validate`), the playbook-driven LLM output pattern (Layer 1 orchestrator template + Layer 2 PromptSchemaRenderer `## Input`), and `DeliverComposite` section-name-keyed streaming (ADR-037). Works within the r2-core boundary + BFF hygiene governance.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A validated "Communication Triage" JPS Action whose structured output (category, urgency, obligations[], suggested actions[], response checklist) is delivered via `DeliverComposite` with section-name-keyed sections per ADR-037, authored per `SPAARKE-PLAYBOOK-LLM-OUTPUT-PATTERN.md`. It runs through `AppOnlyAnalysisService` (app-only/MI; ADR-016 budget, ADR-014 cache) as an AI rung — so it emits `Suggested`/`Ambiguous` only and never auto-files. `jps-validate` passes; build clean; publish-size + CVE reported; `/conflict-check` clean; Placement Justification stated.
  </goal>

  <context>
